# A path of more than one name rooted at a method is one path in every value position (l2_path_chain_check): M\b\v
# is v of the Box in M's field b.  As a `return:` value and as a call's actual -- positions the check does not look
# at -- it used to be the call of M with `\b\v` written out raw after it, C that did not compile.  M sets b\v 5 and
# returns; peek gives M\b\v, and take(M\b\v) + 1.  5 * 10 + 6 = 56 -> success 7; any other value 64.
Box:
    int: v 0
end: Box
fn: M () int
    Box: b
    b\v: 5
    return: 0
end: M
fn: take (int: x) int
    return: x + 1
end: take
fn: peek () int
    return: M\b\v
end: peek
fn: peek2 () int
    return: take(M\b\v)
end: peek2
M()
int: r 0
r: peek() * 10 + peek2()
int: ok 64
if: r = 56
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
